Okay, sure.
好的，没问题。

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.120
First of all, thank you so much.
首先，非常感谢。

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.519
We're, and I'm sorry we made you chase us.
我们……抱歉让你追了我们这么久。

00:07:09.519 --> 00:07:13.360
But this is sometimes, that's how the love story goes.
但有时候，爱情故事就是这样的。

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:16.540
You know, you just, you chase for a while and you finally get us.
你知道的，你追了一阵子，然后终于追到了我们。

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:20.040
This is a pilot that we really loved.
这是一个我们真的很喜欢的试播集。

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:25.040
that we wrote it pitched it and sold it to CBS in 2014, 15?
我们在2014、2015年左右写了它，向CBS推销并卖了出去？

00:07:28.199 --> 00:07:32.160
I think 15 or 16 maybe, something like that, yeah.
我想可能是15或16年吧，差不多那会儿，对。

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:57.560
And it just, it was, I don't know, I don't know, Craig, if you had a different perspective on it, I sort of felt like this whole idea, that sort of the concept behind it, the Craig and I were huge fans of Buffy the Vampire Slayer and just fans, we've been fans of Fantasy and sci-fi for a long time, just especially for me, The particular thing when fantasy and sci-fi serves as a metaphor for something real in real life.
当时就是……我不知道，Craig，如果你有不同的看法的话——我当时觉得整个创意，也就是它背后的概念，我和Craig都是《吸血鬼猎人巴菲》的超级粉丝，而且我们一直以来都是奇幻和科幻作品的粉丝，尤其是对我而言，当奇幻和科幻成为现实生活中某些真实事物的隐喻时，那种感觉特别棒。

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:00.199
And I thought Buffy the Vampire Slayer did that so well.
我觉得《吸血鬼猎人巴菲》在这方面做得太出色了。

00:08:00.199 --> 00:08:08.639
And it sort of felt like this was kind of like how I met your mother meets Buffy the Vampire Slayer, set in New York in a crazy kooky museum.
感觉这就有点像是《老爸老妈浪漫史》遇上了《吸血鬼猎人巴菲》，故事背景设定在纽约一个疯狂又古怪的博物馆里。

00:08:10.839 --> 00:08:29.439
Yeah, we sold it to CBS and I think the script for reading is labeled for CBS because this was the last thing This was the fresh off the personnel transport, dropped into the battle before we started getting the note.
对，我们把它卖给了CBS，我想我们今天用来朗读的剧本上还贴着CBS的标签，因为这是最后的东西——这是刚从人员运输车上下来、还没等我们收到那些修改意见就被投入战斗的版本。

00:08:29.439 --> 00:08:33.159
Like, well, we love the magic, but can you take all the magic out?
就像是：“嗯，我们喜欢魔法，但你们能把所有的魔法都去掉吗？”

00:08:33.159 --> 00:08:34.000
Oh yeah.
哦，对。

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:39.919
And then it went to hell from there, but this is the most magical version of it.
然后情况就急转直下了，但这个版本是其中最具有魔法色彩的版本。

00:08:39.919 --> 00:08:42.879
So the most magic forward version of it.
也就是最强调魔法的版本。

00:08:42.879 --> 00:08:47.120
So yeah, that's kind of what it is.
所以，对，差不多就是这样。

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:50.399
Yeah, I would just add it's definitely, It's like Buffy meets how I'm at your mother.
是的，我只想补充一句，它绝对是……就像是《巴菲》遇上了《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

00:08:50.399 --> 00:08:55.120
We said, how could we do something that's a dating show in New York having already done almost a decade of that?
我们在想，在已经拍了将近十年之后，我们怎么才能在纽约拍一部关于约会的剧集？

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:55.960
How can you do it new?
你要怎么才能拍出新意呢？

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:58.840
Well, let's do Buffy as well, because we love Buffy.
好吧，那就再加上《巴菲》的元素吧，因为我们太爱《巴菲》了。

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:00.919
There's a little bit of Ghostbusters in there.
里面有一点《捉鬼敢死队》的影子。

00:09:00.919 --> 00:09:08.000
Say a little bit of Raiders of the Lost Ark, the idea of sort of collecting things that are somewhat magical and like putting them in a museum and preserving them.
还有点像《夺宝奇兵》，那种收集带点魔法的东西，把它们放进博物馆保存起来的概念。

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:11.399
And there's dating in New York because we're the Harriment of other guys.
而且里面有在纽约的约会桥段，因为我们就是其他男人的“哈里曼”。

00:09:11.399 --> 00:09:15.080
So we tried to do it all and that's why it worked and ran eight seasons away.
所以我们把各种元素都融合进去了，这就是它成功并播了八季的原因。

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.240
It's a dead pilot and we're reading it now.
这是一个流产的试播集，而我们现在正在阅读它。

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.712
Well, it is our pleasure to get to do it.
嗯，我们很高兴能做这件事。

00:09:20.712 --> 00:09:21.559
I'm sorry.
我很抱歉。

00:09:21.559 --> 00:09:25.539
