你对我下咒了吗？

00:33:48.180 --> 00:33:49.019
What?
什么？

00:33:49.019 --> 00:33:52.039
The others watch as Carl and Rachel start arguing.
其他人看着卡尔和瑞秋争吵起来。

00:33:52.039 --> 00:33:53.500
Okay, I'm leaving.
好了，我要走了。

00:33:53.500 --> 00:33:57.180
Nessie stands up and starts to walk away as Rachel and Carl keep arguing.
在瑞秋和卡尔继续争吵的同时，内西站起身准备离开。

00:33:57.180 --> 00:33:59.380
Carl is getting impassioned.
卡尔变得情绪激动起来。

00:33:59.380 --> 00:34:02.779
Just answer the question, are you a witch?
回答我的问题就行，你是不是女巫？

00:34:02.779 --> 00:34:05.140
Can you please not expect the rate in my face?
你能别把唾沫星子喷我脸上行吗？

00:34:05.140 --> 00:34:08.440
Back behind the car, Sam's eyes bolt open.
车后，山姆的眼睛猛地睁大。

00:34:08.440 --> 00:34:10.909
Tell me you all just heard that.
告诉我你们刚才都听到了。

00:34:10.909 --> 00:34:12.510
Nessie, get down!
内西，蹲下！

00:34:12.510 --> 00:34:14.750
You don't know what you're up against.
你根本不知道你在跟什么样的人作对。

00:34:14.750 --> 00:34:15.989
Yes, I do.
不，我知道。

00:34:15.989 --> 00:34:29.949
I am up against my own misguided expectations of what life in New York was going to be like, because instead of working at an actual museum with actual scientists, I'm stuck with a bunch of crackpots who think witches are real, which they are not.
我在跟自己对纽约生活的错误期待作对，因为我没有去真正的博物馆和真正的科学家一起工作，而是被困在了一群以为女巫是真实存在的怪咖中间，然而女巫根本就不存在。

00:34:29.949 --> 00:34:37.030
And just then, across the street, as Carl yells at Rachel, we see Rachel look one way down the block and then the other.
就在这时，街对面，当卡尔朝着瑞秋大喊大叫时，我们看到瑞秋先是朝街区的一头看了一眼，然后又看了看另一头。

00:34:37.030 --> 00:34:38.269
The coast is clear.
周围很安全。

00:34:38.269 --> 00:34:40.550
She takes out a wand and zap.
她掏出一根魔杖，biu的一声。

00:34:40.550 --> 00:34:42.789
She turns Carl into a frog.
她把卡尔变成了一只青蛙。

00:34:42.789 --> 00:34:46.309
Everyone is stunned.
所有人都惊呆了。

00:34:46.309 --> 00:34:49.780
Expectorate, crazy.
吐口水，疯了。

00:34:49.780 --> 00:34:52.739
And that's the end of act two.
第二幕到此结束。

00:34:52.739 --> 00:34:56.539
Hi, I'm Alex Goldman, host of the Hyper-Fixed Podcast.
嗨，我是亚历克斯·戈尔德曼，“超强固定”播客的主持人。

00:34:56.539 --> 00:35:00.059
Each week, we take listeners' problems and try to solve them for them.
每周，我们都会接听听众的问题并尝试为他们解决。

00:35:00.059 --> 00:35:03.219
Problems like, I'm 30 and I'm scared to drive in New York.
比如这些问题：我30岁了，不敢在纽约开车。

00:35:03.219 --> 00:35:06.980
Or why can't I adjust the volume of my car stereo when I'm in reverse?
或者为什么我倒车时不能调节车载音响的音量？

00:35:06.980 --> 00:35:09.500
We also solve non-car related problems.
我们也解决与汽车无关的问题。

00:35:09.500 --> 00:35:15.610
If you have a problem, not only will we fix it, we'll expose the hidden systems that cause that problem in the first place.
如果你遇到了问题，我们不仅会解决它，还会揭开导致该问题的隐藏系统。

00:35:15.610 --> 00:35:18.090
That's the Hyper-Fixed Podcast from Radiotopia.
这就是来自Radiotopia的“超强固定”播客。

00:35:18.090 --> 00:35:27.460
Find it wherever you find podcasts or at HyperFixedPod.com.
你可以在任何收听播客的地方找到它，或者访问 HyperFixedPod.com。

00:35:27.460 --> 00:35:30.179
Act three, we are interior of the belfry.
第三幕，我们在钟楼内部。

00:35:30.179 --> 00:35:33.659
It's the old Irish bar where the museum crew hangs out.
那是博物馆工作人员经常光顾的老牌爱尔兰酒吧。

00:35:33.659 --> 00:35:37.260
Pete, Nessie, Lindsey, and Sam sit, silently drinking beers.
皮特、内西、林赛和萨姆坐着，默默地喝着啤酒。

00:35:37.260 --> 00:35:40.340
In the middle of the table is a large bullfrog.
桌子中央有一只大牛蛙。

00:35:40.340 --> 00:35:43.829
Nessie is in silent shock.
内西陷入了无声的震惊中。

00:35:43.829 --> 00:35:52.070
Well, there's obviously a lot to process here, but speaking purely as a scientist, how cool was that?
好吧，这里显然有很多事情需要消化，但纯粹从科学的角度来看，刚才那有多酷？

00:35:52.070 --> 00:35:55.630
Yeah, I got to turn into a bullfrog peat, not exactly cost for a pizza party.
是啊，我得变成一只牛蛙了，皮特，这可不光是一场披萨派对的费用。

00:35:55.630 --> 00:35:56.493
I don't know.
我不知道。

00:35:56.493 --> 00:35:57.756
Bullfrogs are cool.
牛蛙很酷。

00:35:57.756 --> 00:35:59.750
Maybe she did the guy a favor.
也许她帮了那家伙一个忙。

00:35:59.750 --> 00:36:00.463
A favor?
一个忙？

00:36:00.463 --> 00:36:02.070
He's an amphibian.
他是一只两栖动物。

00:36:02.070 --> 00:36:04.219
Bullfrogs can jump ten times their own height.
牛蛙能跳出自身高度十倍的高度。

00:36:04.219 --> 00:36:06.089
Who wouldn't love to be able to do that?
谁不想有这种能力呢？

00:36:06.089 --> 00:36:06.789
I know I would.
我知道我想。

00:36:06.789 --> 00:36:09.030
You'd rather be a bullfrog than a human being.
你宁愿当一只牛蛙也不愿当人类。

00:36:09.030 --> 00:36:11.429
They catch food with their tongues.
它们用舌头捕捉食物。

00:36:11.429 --> 00:36:12.341
Flies, Sam.
苍蝇，萨姆。

00:36:12.341 --> 00:36:13.750
They catch flies.
它们抓苍蝇。

00:36:13.750 --> 00:36:18.295
Yeah, and to a bullfrog, a fly is like the most delicious thing ever.
对啊，对牛蛙来说，苍蝇就像是有史以来最美味的东西。

00:36:18.295 --> 00:36:20.469
A fly is a bullfrog banana split.
苍蝇就是牛蛙的香蕉船冰淇淋。

00:36:20.469 --> 00:36:25.929
Hey, I wonder if female frogs hate frog Carl.
嘿，我在想母青蛙会不会讨厌青蛙卡尔。

00:36:25.929 --> 00:36:34.280
Nessie, I need you to go down to the pond in Central Park, get three, no, ten female frogs.
内西，我需要你去中央公园的池塘，找三只，不，十只母青蛙。

00:36:34.280 --> 00:36:37.639
Finally, Nessie gets up visibly shaken.
最后，内西站起身来，明显受到了惊吓。

00:36:37.639 --> 00:36:39.639
I'm moving back to Wisconsin.
我要搬回威斯康星州了。

00:36:39.639 --> 00:36:42.139
She starts to leave, but Lindsey stands up.
她正要离开，但林赛站了起来。

00:36:42.139 --> 00:36:46.349
Well, so you're just leaving?
好吧，所以你就要走了？

00:36:46.349 --> 00:36:48.849
As soon as possible, yes.
越快越好，是的。

00:36:48.849 --> 00:36:52.550
But I thought we had a nice little friendship form in here.
但我以为我们在这里建立了一段美好的友谊。

00:36:52.550 --> 00:36:54.059
What?
什么？

00:36:54.059 --> 00:36:57.639
All you do is make fun of me.
你只会取笑我。

00:36:57.639 --> 00:36:59.880
That's how you treat your friends.
这就是你对待朋友的方式。

00:36:59.880 --> 00:37:02.139
How does it work in Wisconsin?
威斯康星州是怎样的？

00:37:02.139 --> 00:37:03.619
Nessie shakes her head and exits.
内西摇了摇头，走了出去。

00:37:03.619 --> 00:37:07.179
The waitress appears and looks at the bullfrog, kind of perplexed.
女服务员出现，看着牛蛙，有点困惑。

00:37:07.179 --> 00:37:08.179
After a beat.
过了一拍。

00:37:08.179 --> 00:37:10.179
Marl.
马尔。

00:37:10.179 --> 00:37:12.719
We go to the river walk.
我们来到河滨步道。

00:37:12.719 --> 00:37:16.380
Nessie is walking along the river on her phone.
内西一边打着电话，一边沿着河边走着。

00:37:16.380 --> 00:37:17.380
Mom.
妈妈。

00:37:17.380 --> 00:37:18.860
Sam catches up with her.
萨姆追上了她。

00:37:18.860 --> 00:37:19.860
No, Nessie, no.
不，内西，不。

00:37:19.860 --> 00:37:20.860
Hang up the phone.
挂断电话。

00:37:20.860 --> 00:37:22.179
He tries to take the phone from her.
他试图从她手中抢过手机。

00:37:22.179 --> 00:37:23.780
They wrestle for it.
他们为之争夺。

00:37:23.780 --> 00:37:25.380
No, Mom, I'm not being mugged.
不，妈妈，我没有被抢劫。

00:37:25.380 --> 00:37:27.300
It's just this weird guy I work with.
只是和我一起工作的这个怪人。

00:37:27.300 --> 00:37:28.699
This is for your own good.
这是为了你好。

00:37:28.699 --> 00:37:34.260
In the struggle, the phone goes flying into the East River, splash, a long beat, and then...
在挣扎中，手机飞进了东河，扑通一声，过了好一会儿，然后……

00:37:34.260 --> 00:37:37.170
Okay, we need to get a bag of rice.
好吧，我们需要一袋大米。

00:37:37.170 --> 00:37:39.210
You owe me a phone.
你欠我一部手机。

00:37:39.210 --> 00:37:42.750
Yes, I owe you a phone, but hear me out.
是的，我欠你一部手机，但听我解释。

00:37:42.750 --> 00:37:44.070
You can't leave.
你不能走。

00:37:44.070 --> 00:37:44.889
You can't give up.
你不能放弃。

00:37:44.889 --> 00:37:47.150
New York is rough, no doubt.
纽约很残酷，毫无疑问。

00:37:47.150 --> 00:37:49.550
When it's cold, it is up, yours cold.
冷的时候，冷得要死。

00:37:49.550 --> 00:37:52.349
When it's hot, it is screw you hot and yes.
热的时候，热得见鬼，而且是的。

00:37:52.349 --> 00:37:55.150
Sometimes people get turned into frogs.
有时人们会变成青蛙。

00:37:55.150 --> 00:37:57.590
There is dark magic here, no doubt.
这里有黑魔法，毫无疑问。

00:37:57.590 --> 00:37:59.389
But there's also good magic.
但也有善良的魔法。

00:37:59.389 --> 00:38:00.230
I mean...
我是说……

00:38:00.230 --> 00:38:05.869
He gestures off camera and we swing around to a postcard view of the Brooklyn Bridge, then right back to Nessie.
他指了指镜头外，我们转向布鲁克林大桥的明信片视角，然后又转回内西。

00:38:05.869 --> 00:38:08.110
The view has the desired effect on her.
这个景色对她产生了预期的效果。

00:38:08.110 --> 00:38:10.510
She softens for a moment and then...
她平静了一会儿，然后……

00:38:10.510 --> 00:38:12.030
Okay.
好吧。

00:38:12.030 --> 00:38:14.539
Yes, beautiful bridge.
是的，桥很美。

00:38:14.539 --> 00:38:16.219
But witches?
但是巫婆呢？

00:38:16.219 --> 00:38:19.219
That stuff just doesn't happen in green leaf.
这种事在格林利夫根本不会发生。

00:38:19.219 --> 00:38:20.940
Neither does that stuff.
那种事也不会。

00:38:20.940 --> 00:38:29.820
He points to the bridge, and again, we swing around to a postcard shot, only this time in the foreground, a two-foot-long rat emerges from a trash can and scurries away.
他指着桥，我们再次转向明信片镜头，只是这次在前景中，一只两英尺长的老鼠从垃圾桶里钻出来，匆忙逃跑。

00:38:29.820 --> 00:38:34.519
Nessie screams it's terrifying, back on Nessie and Sam holding each other.
内西尖叫着，太可怕了，镜头切回内西和萨姆互相拥抱。

00:38:34.519 --> 00:38:36.440
Oh my God, that is gonna give me nightmares.
噢天哪，这会给我留下噩梦的。

00:38:36.440 --> 00:38:51.019
That really well, look, Sam stops himself from gagging and then, oh, look, New York isn't the guarantee that something great is gonna happen, But it is the chance that it might at any moment.
这真的——好吧，听着，萨姆强忍住恶心然后，噢，听着，纽约并不能保证一定会有什么伟大的事情发生，但它确实提供了随时可能发生的机遇。

00:38:51.019 --> 00:38:56.460
And if you ask me, that's worth a few witches and rats.
如果你问我，这绝对值得几个女巫和老鼠。

00:38:56.460 --> 00:38:59.019
And whatever that creepy, heavy set gentleman is doing over there in the bushes.
还有那个在灌木丛里鬼鬼祟祟、胖乎乎的绅士在做的那种事。

00:38:59.019 --> 00:39:00.159
Oh, don't look.
噢，别看。

00:39:00.159 --> 00:39:03.639
Nessie can't help but smile at this.
内西看到这里忍不住笑了。

00:39:03.639 --> 00:39:07.800
New York needs people with good magic inside them, Nessie.
纽约需要内心充满善良魔法的人，内西。

00:39:07.800 --> 00:39:09.730
Or else we're lost.
否则我们就迷失了。

00:39:09.730 --> 00:39:11.539
New York needs you.
纽约需要你。

00:39:11.539 --> 00:39:14.900
Off Nessie thinking about this, we go to the belfry.
看着内西陷入沉思，我们来到了钟楼。

00:39:14.900 --> 00:39:18.900
Lindsay and Pete continue to ponder frog philosophy.
林赛和皮特继续思考青蛙哲学。

00:39:18.900 --> 00:39:20.500
Oh, sack up, Lindsay.
噢，振作点，林赛。

00:39:20.500 --> 00:39:23.340
Middle school science classes do it all the time.
初中科学课一直都这么做。

00:39:23.340 --> 00:39:26.099
You are not gonna dissect Carl.
你不会解剖卡尔的。

00:39:26.099 --> 00:39:29.579
Just then, Nessie rushes in, grabs the frog and runs out.
就在这时，内西冲了进来，抓起青蛙跑了出去。

00:39:29.579 --> 00:39:32.420
On the street, Nessie marches up to Rachel's door.
在街上，内西大步走到瑞秋的门前。

00:39:32.420 --> 00:39:34.900
Pete, Lindsay, and Sam catch up to her.
皮特、林赛和萨姆追了上来。

00:39:34.900 --> 00:39:35.860
Nessie, wait.
内西，等等。

00:39:35.860 --> 00:39:36.699
But it's too late.
但已经太迟了。

00:39:36.699 --> 00:39:38.179
She rings the doorbell.
她按响了门铃。

00:39:38.179 --> 00:39:39.099
Hide.
躲起来。

00:39:39.099 --> 00:39:44.139
Pete, Lindsay, and Sam hide behind a car as Rachel answers the door, still holding her phone to her ear.
皮特、林赛和萨姆躲在一辆车后面，瑞秋则接起门铃对讲机，手里依然拿着电话贴在耳边。

00:39:44.139 --> 00:39:47.590
Behind her we see pictures of her kids on the wall.
在她身后的墙上，能看到她孩子的照片。

00:39:47.590 --> 00:39:49.099
Can I help you?
有什么需要帮忙的吗？

00:39:49.099 --> 00:39:51.500
Yes, you can.
是的，确实有。

00:39:51.500 --> 00:39:53.780
You turned my friend into a frog.
你把我朋友变成了一只青蛙。

00:39:53.780 --> 00:39:55.659
Yes, he holds up the frog.
没错，他举起了那只青蛙。

00:39:55.659 --> 00:39:57.699
Look, I just moved here this week.
听着，我这周才刚搬到这里。

00:39:57.699 --> 00:40:01.019
Maybe you don't remember what that first week in New York is like.
也许你不记得在纽约的第一周是什么感觉了。

00:40:01.019 --> 00:40:05.420
My first week in New York, my whole family was murdered by Indians.
我刚到纽约的第一周，我的全家都被印第安人杀害了。

00:40:05.420 --> 00:40:08.269
It was 1631.
那是1631年。

00:40:08.269 --> 00:40:10.949
Okay, Native Americans.
好吧，是美洲原住民。

00:40:10.949 --> 00:40:14.190
But yes, exactly, it sucks.
但没错，就是这样，这感觉糟透了。

00:40:14.190 --> 00:40:17.889
But now, you live in a fricking pottery barn catalog.
但现在，你居然住在一个活生生的陶器巴恩商品目录风的屋子里。

00:40:17.889 --> 00:40:19.929
You're living the dream.
你正过着梦想中的生活。

00:40:19.929 --> 00:40:22.250
Isn't it time to let bygones be bygones?
难道不该让过去的就过去吗？

00:40:23.409 --> 00:40:25.480
No.
不。

00:40:25.480 --> 00:40:27.840
Yes, it is.
不，应该让它过去。

00:40:27.840 --> 00:40:29.820
No, it isn't.
不，不应该。

00:40:29.820 --> 00:40:30.960
Rachel's eyes narrow.
瑞秋的眼睛眯了起来。

00:40:30.960 --> 00:40:32.599
The wind starts to blow a little.
风开始微微刮起。

00:40:32.599 --> 00:40:33.440
Uh-oh.
噢哦。

00:40:33.440 --> 00:40:38.000
Behind the car across the street, Lindsey, Pete, and Sam watch the action unfold.
在街对面的车后，林赛、皮特和萨姆注视着事态的发展。

00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:39.840
Guys, we gotta help her.
伙计们，我们得帮帮她。

00:40:39.840 --> 00:40:41.079
Absolutely not.
绝对不行。

00:40:41.079 --> 00:40:43.039
Do you wanna get turned into a frog, too?
你也想变成青蛙吗？

00:40:43.039 --> 00:40:44.800
Yeah, kinda.
好吧，有点想。

00:40:44.800 --> 00:40:47.800
Sam runs to join Nessie as she yells at Rachel.
萨姆跑过去加入内西，此时内西正冲着瑞秋大喊。

00:40:47.800 --> 00:40:51.800
Oh, and now you're going to cast some spell on me.
哦，现在你又打算对我施什么咒语了吗？

00:40:51.800 --> 00:40:52.800
Is that it?
是这样吗？

00:40:52.800 --> 00:40:55.800
You know, everyone back in Wisconsin thinks New Yorkers are mean.
你知道的，威斯康星老家的每个人都觉得纽约人很刻薄。

00:40:55.800 --> 00:40:57.800
Are you really going to prove them right?
你真的打算用实际行动证明他们是对的吗？

00:40:57.800 --> 00:40:59.800
Rachel's eyes glow red.
瑞秋的眼睛发出了红光。

00:40:59.800 --> 00:41:01.800
Sam steps in front of Nessie.
萨姆挡在了内西身前。

00:41:01.800 --> 00:41:02.800
Get behind me, Nessie.
躲到我身后去，内西。

00:41:02.800 --> 00:41:04.800
If anyone gets to be a frog, it's me.
如果非得有人变成青蛙，那也得是我。

00:41:04.800 --> 00:41:06.800
Gets to.
还“非得”。

00:41:06.800 --> 00:41:10.800
No, I mean, I don't want to be a frog at all or a dolphin.
不，我的意思是，我根本不想变成青蛙，也不想变成海豚。

00:41:10.800 --> 00:41:12.800
Sam is clearly pretty excited.
萨姆显然相当兴奋。

00:41:12.800 --> 00:41:15.930
